# VTID-03940 — commands run during this change

## Investigation (via Explore subagent, then independently verified)
Confirmed via grep that buildContextSignalFromMemory() is a real, live call
site (routes/orb-live.ts imports and invokes it, `context_bundle:
memoryContext?.ok ? buildContextSignalFromMemory({...`), not dead code.
Confirmed zero pre-existing test files for this module:
$ find services/gateway/test -iname "intent-detection-engine*"
(no results, before this VTID)

Found the sibling precedent in services/navigator-consult.ts's
buildMemoryHints(): `cat === 'conversation' || cat === 'notes'` →
push content, capped at 3. Followed the same category convention here,
capped at 5 to match this function's own personal_facts.slice(0, 5).

## Fix
Extended buildContextSignalFromMemory()'s existing item loop
(services/gateway/src/services/intent-detection-engine.ts) to also
collect conversation/notes items into recentTopics, truncated to 100
chars, capped at 5. Removed the `recent_topics: []` TODO stub.

## New test file (written from scratch — no existing coverage to extend)
services/gateway/test/intent-detection-engine.test.ts — 8 tests: the two
existing no-op guards (ok:false, empty items), personal_facts unchanged,
the actual recent_topics fix, no-regression when no conversation/notes
items exist, the 5-item cap, the 100-char truncation, and
memory_categories/memory_item_count unaffected.

Initially wrote the file referencing a provisional VTID-03939 before
actually allocating — the allocator returned VTID-03940 instead (another
session claimed 03939 in this active shared repo in the interim).
Corrected via sed across the test file before committing; no VTID-03939
references remain.

